    <span class="eyebrow">The work</span>
    <h2>Three ways of getting useful things done.</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card"><span class="num">01 · ADVISE</span><h3>Commercial and regulatory judgment.</h3><p>Helping businesses and investors navigate Greece and Cyprus, regulated markets and cross-border execution.</p><a href="/work">See the practice ↗</a></article>
      <article class="card"><span class="num">02 · SERVE</span><h3>Public responsibility, close to delivery.</h3><p>Municipal councillor and former deputy mayor in Galatsi — elected 10th among 400+ candidates and working where policy meets budgets, systems and citizens.</p><a href="/public-contribution">See public life ↗</a></article>
      <article class="card"><span class="num">03 · BUILD</span><h3>Better information for better buying.</h3><p>Founder of Procura, exploring how market research can improve public procurement before a tender begins.</p><a href="https://www.procura.gr/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Visit Procura ↗</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band"><div class="wrap split"><div><span class="eyebrow">A useful conversation</span></div><div><h2>Bring the real problem. We can work out the rest.</h2><p>If your project sits between business, government and technology, I may be useful at the point where analysis has to become action.</p><a class="button" href="mailto:andreoulegal@gmail.com">Start a conversation ↗</a></div></div></section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="ideas">
    <span class="eyebrow">Ideas in development</span>
    <h2>Questions worth staying with.</h2>
    <div class="list">
      <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Why public procurement fails before the tender begins.</h3><p>Market understanding, incentives and the design decisions hidden before a formal process starts.</p></div><b>↗</b></article>
      <article><span>02</span><div><h3>What local government teaches us about digital transformation.</h3><p>Technology is only useful when the institution around it can absorb and sustain change.</p></div><b>↗</b></article>
      <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Why businesses need to understand institutions, not only markets.</h3><p>Regulation, trust and public value are part of the operating environment.</p></div><b>↗</b></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
